e third largest on earth  located 14 000 feet above sea level  they belong to the highest geothermal  field in the world  at these altitudes water is a little  easier to come by  than in the deserts heartlands  snow melt from the nearby mountains  collects and forms small lakes on the  altiplano  at this altitude there are strange  creatures that call the water pools home  the giant coot lives up to its name  this water bird weighs 5 pounds  [Music]  huge feet allow them to carry their bulk  over floating weeds without sinking  this male is looking for building  material  giant coots are house proud  their entire day is dedicated to  constructing their nest  they work together with their partners  spending hours adding to the structure  with plants they've torn up from the  lake bed  [Music]  there's a lot at stake for these  homeowners  trespassing isn't tolerated  [Music]  yet some coots aren't willing to put in  the time to do their own home  improvements  [Music]  nest looting in this neighborhood is  rife  [Music]  enough's enough this kud isn't having it  [Music]  he sets his sights on the latest thief  and charges after  him giant coots can't really fly  but their incredibly powerful legs and  huge crab-like feet  allow them to blaze through the water  when the homeowner catches up with the  thief he initiates the coot version  of kickboxing  though this might look silly there's a  lot of power behind  each slap the claws on the end of the  coot's feet  are incredibly sharp  in the chaos of the fight they've  trespassed onto another neighbor's  territory  [Music]  the fight has now escalated into a brawl  [Music]  finally exhausted everyone cools off  but the piece will definitely be  short-lived with tempers like these  as the sun sets shadows in chile's  altiplano stretch their way up the banks  of the andes  meanwhile in the desert's dry and dusty  interior  an unlikely animal remains wide awake  in the middle of chile's atacama desert  the skies are clear