ert  are replaced by rich emerald  this unexpected good fortune for the  animals of the atacama  attracts visitors to the fertile plains  a south american gray fox is here to  hunt down a mate  for the first time in his life  the desert can be a lonely place and the  drive to reproduce  is all-consuming  [Music]  he might have only one shot at finding a  mate this season  so it's important to be thorough  a stranger to this area he makes his  mark on every surface available  this scent trail is the fox's version of  a flag  he's staking a claim to the territory  and  access to any females in it  [Music]  [Music]  it seems he's found a lead on a local  lady  he lets out a greeting  out here the sound travels for miles  [Music]  the female hears him  uncertain if he's a threat she's  cautious  she provides him with a coded message  [Music]  her urine reveals her reproductive  status  it's the beginning of courtship  proceedings  [Music]  finally he tracks her down before he can  approach  he demonstrates submission so she  understands his intentions  but he's a little over eager and she's  not making it easy  wrapping her tail around her body is her  way of denying him  [Music]  he'll have to try harder than this if he  wants to win her over  [Music]  it's going to be an exhausting few days  [Music]  if he forgets to pay attention to her  she has ways of reminding him to up his  game  [Music]  this pair will remain together for five  more months  before they go their separate ways in  that time  with any luck they'll leave behind a  legacy in the form  of up to four offspring  the rains have provided a temporary  relief from desolate dust lands  but there are many places in the atacama  that have no hope of seeing water  falling from the sky  instead life here has to source moisture  from the ground  but that's easier said than done  the salar de pintaros is an ancient lake  bed  the soil has extremely high  concentrations of salt  [Music]  it's nearly impossible for 